                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "What a putrid sequel to a legendary game, this is awfull. The last stage was an advertisement to the developpers other game NUX from the level itself down to the enemies everthing was a ctrlC ctrlV from NUX. Screaming eyeballs alien uclers to pop under horror music inside an alien. This was nothing that the Original Platypus' dev wanted Athony Flack the developer of the original game was discusted by the sequel. Even the final boss was copied from NUX. Not to mention the constant anoying references to NUX ie protagonist ship in the background, that laughing bastard from the nux logo on stage one. \n\nThe ENDING IS A BLATANT NAG SCREEN TO BUY NUX, this is not worth your time.\n\nAS much as i loved the original i hate the sequel on the same level\n\nGo and get Platypus 1 THe ORIGINAL if you want a good game.\n\nStay away from this sh*t",
